<title>JAPAN: Japan Sept tin imports up 0.3 pct year/year.</title>
<headline>Japan Sept tin imports up 0.3 pct year/year.</headline>
<dateline>TOKYO 1996-10-29</dateline>
<text>
<p>Japan imported 1,887 tonnes of</p>
<p>refined tin in September, up 0.3 percent from 1,881 tonnes in</p>
<p>the same month last year, Finance Ministry data showed on</p>
<p>Tuesday.</p>
<p>The imports (on a customs-cleared basis in tonnes) were as</p>
<p>follows:</p>
<p>		     Sept 96	  Aug 96	  Sept 95</p>
<p> Total		1,887	    2,250	    1,881</p>
<p>Major suppliers:</p>
<p> Indonesia	    818	    1,157		836</p>
<p> Malaysia	     557		521		600</p>
<p>Cumulative imports in the first nine months of 1996 were 18,930 tonnes, versus 61,633 tonnes in the same period last year.</p>
<p>--Tokyo Commodities Desk (81-3 3432 6179)</p>
</text>
